WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.722
Use timing to distinguish these repair processes. During copying, DNA polymerase can catch

00:00:04.722 --> 00:00:09.444
a wrong base it just added. Its exonuclease activity removes that incorrect base

00:00:09.444 --> 00:00:14.167
from the three prime end.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:18.750
After replication is complete, mismatch repair proteins scan the new double helix. When

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:23.333
they find a mismatch, enzymes remove the affected section and replace it with

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:27.917
the correct DNA nucleotides.

00:00:27.917 --> 00:00:32.917
Proofreading is a check during copying by DNA polymerase itself. Mismatch repair is

00:00:32.917 --> 00:00:37.917
a check after replication. Both correct mistakes, but the timing and the proteins

00:00:37.917 --> 00:00:42.917
doing the checking distinguish the two processes.
